The documentation for XPilot NG is far from complete.

For further reading, see the manuals in the doc/man directory.



GAMEPLAY TRANSPORT

Gameplay connections use UDP by default.  To use TCP, start both endpoints
with `-gameTransport tcp`, for example:

        xpilot-ng-server -gameTransport tcp [other options]
        xpilot-ng-sdl -gameTransport tcp -join server.example

The client and server must select the same value (`udp` or `tcp`); there is no
automatic fallback.  The `-port` option continues to identify the UDP contact
port.  LAN discovery, metaserver, and lobby paths are unchanged.  The
`clientPortStart` and `clientPortEnd` range applies to the selected gameplay
protocol on the server and to the client's contact and gameplay sockets.

TCP gameplay records contain a two-byte network-order payload length followed
by an unchanged XPilot packet payload.  Server recordings must be replayed
with the same `gameTransport` value that was used while recording.



